Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:12:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] Flash Next CUDA: the hyper-connection normalize over
 256-column slices

fn_hc_normalize ran one block a (row, stream): at one decode row four blocks scaled 10,240 values
while thread 0 summed the stream's partials. fn_hc_normalize_cols takes a block a (row, stream,
256-column slice); each block sums the same partials in the same order, so every value's bits are
fn_hc_normalize's, with forty blocks a decode row. The old kernel stays (the contract's baseline).

Contract: replaces fn_hc_normalize bit for bit (gates 1-3; gate 4 states the bf16 sum it cannot
show through the root), its control the new kernel with a doubled epsilon (red at gate 3).
Served (FP4-Local, no drafts): 23.83 / 23.83 tok/s one stream (main 23.58 / 23.66), replies equal.

(cherry picked from commit 388acff677218fab6256734927bd23f1bd4c9749)
